Chapter: Fat16Mkdir
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 BACKLOG 7.15: a Codex program can create a directory. create-directory was a
 compiler builtin whose emitter raised CDX2043 and explained that the parent
 walk and the dot entries were not written. That was honest, and an honest
 refusal is still a refusal. The name is out of the builtin tables now and the
 work is in Foreword chapter Fat16, next to write-file and file-exists, for the
 same reason they are: the machine does not know what a directory is, and FAT16
 does.

 This starts from a volume with no subdirectory at all -- unlike fat16-subdir,
 whose /SUB is built host-side -- so every directory here was made by the code
 under test. That is the point: the read-back walks a tree this chapter built.

 The assertions worth naming:

 "twice" must be False. Making a directory that exists would otherwise claim a
 second cluster and commit a second entry under the same name: two directories,
 one name, and a walk that finds whichever comes first.

 "nested" and "write-deep" are the ones that would fail if the dot entries were
 wrong. fat16-poke-dir-entry writes an 8.3 name by splitting on the first dot,
 which turns "." into an empty base and an empty extension -- eleven spaces. A
 directory built that way lists fine and cannot be climbed out of, so the dot
 names are poked as literal bytes instead. Two levels deep is what exercises
 the walk that would fall over.

 "no-parent" pins the refusal, because writing a directory entry into a parent
 that does not exist is the corruption this would otherwise cause quietly.

 The harness checks the raw bytes host-side as well: '.' is 2E followed by ten
 spaces and points at its own cluster, '..' is 2E 2E followed by nine and
 points at 0 when the parent is the root, which is the spec's convention and
 not the root's actual sector. A round trip through our own reader cannot see
 either of those being wrong.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    vol <- fat16-init 2048

    made <- fat16-create-directory vol "CFG"
    print-line-uni ("made " & show made)

    e <- fat16-resolve-path vol "CFG"
    print-line-uni ("resolve " & describe e)

    again <- fat16-create-directory vol "CFG"
    print-line-uni ("twice " & show again)

    w <- fat16-write-file "CFG/APP.TXT" "in a made dir"
    print-line-uni ("write-into " & show w)

    back <- fat16-read-text vol "CFG/APP.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("readback " & maybe-text back)

    nested <- fat16-create-directory vol "CFG/SUB2"
    print-line-uni ("nested " & show nested)

    w2 <- fat16-write-file "CFG/SUB2/DEEP.TXT" "two levels"
    print-line-uni ("write-deep " & show w2)

    back2 <- fat16-read-text vol "CFG/SUB2/DEEP.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("readback-deep " & maybe-text back2)

    orphan <- fat16-create-directory vol "NOPE/X"
    print-line-uni ("no-parent " & show orphan)
  end

Section: Reporting

  maybe-text : Maybe Text -> Text
  maybe-text (m) = when m
    is Just (t) -> t
    is None -> "<none>"

  describe : Maybe Fat16DirEntry -> Text
  describe (m) = when m
    is Just (e) -> e.de-name & " attr=" & show (e.de-attr) & " isdir=" & show (bit-and (e.de-attr) 16 == 16)
    is None -> "<none>"
